  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, VRChat, quite frankly, sucks for being able to failover from one WAN connection to another. If I'm in the middle of gameplay and my network goes down and fails over from my first WAN connection to my second one, VRChat boots me then forces me to log back in.\n\nLikewise, if I'm using my phone as a modem and unplug hte phone and plug it back in the same thing happens.\n\nI understand there's security reasons for wanting to force a user to re-authenticate if they suddenly re-log in from an IP address that's hundreds of miles away from the previous one, but this gets a bit frustrating.\n\nHaving to re-log back in constantly on the app or in unity because of a connection failover (or just plain using a different connection) wastes a lot of times, especially if you're using a super-secure password. \n\nHaving the server \"remember\" common connections would be useful.",
